{"parentUuid":"ecaf501a-801a-43f2-926f-8a03ee0d93f1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"aec9dfe82ab5889ef","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015jBRZKiGFwd9BJkMV4hjEg","type":"tool_result","content":"# Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** \"Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming: Boosted Lagrangian Decomposition with Self-Supervised Learning\"\n\n**Authors:** Swann Bessa, Darius Dabert, Max Bourgeat, Louis-Martin Rousseau, Quentin Cappart\n\n**Publication Status:** Submitted to arXiv on August 22, 2024 (arXiv:2408.12695). No conference venue information is listed on this page.\n\n**Core Focus:** Yes, this work directly addresses your question. The paper proposes using neural networks with self-supervised learning to generate Lagrangian multipliers for constraint programming problems. As the abstract states, the authors aim to \"reduce the number of sub-gradient optimization steps required, enhancing the pruning efficiency\" in branch-and-bound solvers.\n\n**Key Innovation:** The authors describe this as \"the first generic method for learning valid dual bounds in constraint programming,\" addressing computational limitations of traditional sub-gradient methods in this domain."}]},"uuid":"4b4bec0b-022e-4db1-9da3-b34c843b617f","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:51:46.740Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ecaf501a-801a-43f2-926f-8a03ee0d93f1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2b948cfb-f63f-4c55-a781-3dcfec25e6d8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"aec9dfe82ab5889ef","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AzCgT7UK22AK9JciseqgG5","type":"tool_result","content":"# PB Competition 2025 Participating Solvers\n\n## Listed Solvers\nYes, the solvers you mentioned are all documented as participants:\n\n- **Exact** and **Exact_proof** - with solver descriptions and source code provided\n- **PRINTEMPS** - \"Pseudo_Boolean_Competition_2025\" description available\n- **NaPS** and **SCIP-NaPS** - with solver description and home page\n- **SCIP** - with solver home page link\n- **roundingsat** - with author home page listed\n\nAdditional participating solvers include AI448PBSolver, LSIPExact, mixed-bag-2024, pb-oll-rs-2024, OR-Tools CP-SAT, Picat, Sat4j Resolution VeriPB, toulbar2, UWrMaxSat, and WMaxCDCL-SCIP.\n\n## Certificate Tracks\n\nThe competition features \"four tracks...opened unconditionally: PBS (PB Satisfaction) and PBO (PB Optimization) for linear constraints, with and without certificate of unsatisfiability/optimality.\"\n\nThere is **no separate epsilon-gap certificate track** mentioned. Only OPT/UNSAT certificates generated in VeriPB format are specified. Both certified and non-certified tracks exist for the two main problem types (satisfaction and optimization)."}]},"uuid":"ada7fd9c-72b3-4699-90c0-41676dfdeac9","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:51:48.900Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2b948cfb-f63f-4c55-a781-3dcfec25e6d8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"398b1fcc-8e64-4b1d-9aae-5335d249a522","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"aec9dfe82ab5889ef","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ydnmdeNgtRB6XYWNcx8Gz","type":"tool_result","content":"# PDF Analysis\n\nI appreciate the request, but the content provided is a **corrupted or compressed PDF file** that cannot be properly parsed. The raw PDF stream contains binary/compressed data that isn't human-readable.\n\nTo answer your questions accurately, I would need:\n- A properly decoded/uncompressed version of the document, or\n- A text-based version of the paper\n\n**What I can observe:**\nThe PDF metadata suggests this is an academic paper (references to sections like \"Proof Logging for Linear Programming Integration\" and \"Pseudo-Boolean Core-Guided Optimization\" appear in the table of contents), but I cannot reliably extract:\n- The exact title\n- Author names\n- Abstract content\n- Claims about industrial usability\n- Support for specific certificate types (epsilon-bound, anytime, intermediate gap)\n\n**Recommendation:**\nPlease provide either:\n1. A readable PDF version\n2. The paper's text/HTML version\n3. A DOI or arXiv link\n\nThis will allow me to give you precise answers about pseudo-boolean optimization proof logging and certificate support.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 1.3MB) also saved to /home/zhuran24/.claude/projects/-home-zhuran24-claude-pj-zmd/7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9/tool-results/webfetch-1778370701282-5k5x84.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"d13bc5c1-4ec1-4da5-ba2c-8d7e9e59395f","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:51:49.742Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"398b1fcc-8e64-4b1d-9aae-5335d249a522","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
