{"parentUuid":"de0fb834-2030-46f5-9a44-4702c50620cc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"aec9dfe82ab5889ef","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qte4QKAdwSi4xBFEs2TLqm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Bessa \"Boosted Lagrangian Decomposition\" AAAI 2025 accepted\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"dblp: Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming: Boosted Lagrangian Decomposition with Self-Supervised Learning.\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/rec/conf/aaai/BessaDBRC25.html\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming: Boosted Lagrangian Decomposition with Self-Supervised Learning | Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/33208\"},{\"title\":\"Corail Research Group - Publications\",\"url\":\"https://corail-research.github.io/publications/\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming:\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/33208/35363\"},{\"title\":\"[2408.12695] Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming: Boosted Lagrangian Decomposition with Self-Supervised Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.12695\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming: Boosted Lagrangian Decomposition with Self-Supervised Learning - PolyPublie\",\"url\":\"https://publications.polymtl.ca/64489/\"},{\"title\":\"Learning valid dual bounds in constraint programming | Proceedings of the Thirty-Ninth AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Thirty-Seventh Conference on Innovative Applications of Artificial Intelligence and Fifteenth Symposium on Educational Advances in Artificial Intelligence\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1609/aaai.v39i11.33208\"},{\"title\":\"Swann Bessa\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=IJrVw5QAAAAJ&hl=fr\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming: Boosted Lagrangian Decomposition with Self-Supervised Learning | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/383413181_Learning_Valid_Dual_Bounds_in_Constraint_Programming_Boosted_Lagrangian_Decomposition_with_Self-Supervised_Learning\"},{\"title\":\"View of Lagrangian Decomposition for Optimal Cost Partitioning\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/ICAPS/article/view/3496/3364\"}]\n\nThe search was successful! I found information about the paper you're looking for.\n\nThe paper \"Learning Valid Dual Bounds in Constraint Programming: Boosted Lagrangian Decomposition with Self-Supervised Learning\" by Swann Bessa, Darius Dabert, Max Bourgeat, Louis-Martin Rousseau, and Quentin Cappart was accepted to AAAI 2025 (pages 11113-11121).\n\nThe paper focuses on Lagrangian decomposition (LD), a relaxation method that provides dual bounds for constrained optimization problems by decomposing them into manageable sub-problems, where Lagrangian multipliers are adjusted iteratively to find the tightest bound. The authors propose a self-supervised learning approach that leverages neural networks to generate multipliers directly, yielding tight bounds.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"21936e75-4983-45bb-b212-e28e11d7148a","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:52:20.026Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"de0fb834-2030-46f5-9a44-4702c50620cc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1b5d31c9-eec0-4c22-894e-3be3966ec3be","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"aec9dfe82ab5889ef","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cfp7NYTLaiLYQJgvrfzG1k","type":"tool_result","content":"# Analysis of SLS-Enhanced Core-Boosted Linear Search Paper\n\nBased on the provided abstract and document content, **the paper does not mention plateau detection, dynamic phase switching, or core-boosted vs SLS phase transition triggered by stagnation**.\n\nThe abstract describes the paper's approach as follows:\n\n> \"Core-boosted linear search is a three-phase algorithm where each phase uses different types of reasoning.\"\n\nHowever, the abstract does not specify what triggers transitions between these phases. It emphasizes that the authors integrated SLS techniques with all three phases and created \"non-trivial information exchange in both directions between the SLS algorithm and the reasoning methods,\" but the specific mechanisms for phase switching are not disclosed in the abstract or metadata provided.\n\nThe focus appears to be on **tight integration and bidirectional communication** between SLS and SAT-based methods rather than on stagnation-detection mechanisms for phase transitions."}]},"uuid":"72720243-7e04-44bc-9ac5-c0b2c730fa9d","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:52:20.859Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1b5d31c9-eec0-4c22-894e-3be3966ec3be","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
