{"parentUuid":"c2eca0f9-4991-4795-b6ed-05de29498760","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"aec9dfe82ab5889ef","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019dVtNFoywEAGwgR72fs2fd","type":"tool_result","content":"240\t\n241\t\fO. Lübke and J. Berg\n242\t\n243\t2.3\n244\t\n245\t28:5\n246\t\n247\tCore-Boosted Linear Search for Anytime MaxSAT\n248\t\n249\tFigure 1 overviews core-boosted linear search for computing a low-cost solution to a (clausebased) MaxSAT instance (FH , FS , w) [10]. Core-boosted search consists of three separate\n250\tphases: preprocessing, core-guided search, and solution-improving search. Each phase can –\n251\tin theory – find and identify an optimal solution to the instance. More importantly, each\n252\tphase will also modify and simplify the instance, and the following phase is always invoked\n253\ton the modified instance rather than the original one. Intuitively, this allows core-boosted\n254\tsearch never to be much worse than any individual phase, while also allowing subsequent\n255\tphases to benefit from deductions made in previous ones. We next detail all three phases.\n256\t\n257\tThe Preprocessing Phase\n258\tThe preprocessing phase converts the input clause-based instance (FH , FS , w) into an\n259\tobjective-based one using the transformation outlined in Section 2.1. Additionally, the\n260\tstep applies different simplification techniques. These can range from removing tautologies\n261\tand reusing unit soft clauses as objective terms to more sophisticated preprocessing rules\n262\tused in SAT and MaxSAT solving, including bounded variable elimination and subsumed\n263\tlabel elimination [8, 25]. For the correctness of core-boosted linear search, we assume that\n264\tthe preprocessing techniques are cost-preserving.\n265\t▶ Definition 3. Invoke the preprocessing phase on an instance (FH , FS , w) and assume\n266\tit returns the instance (F, O + lb1 ) where lb1 is a constant. The preprocessing phase is\n267\tcost-preserving if both of the following hold:\n268\t(i) If αP is a solution of F then there exists a solution α to FH for which cost(FS , w, α) ≤\n269\tαP (O) + lb1 .\n270\t(ii) If α is a solution of FH then there exists a solution αP to F for which αP (O) + lb1 =\n271\tcost(FS , w, α).\n272\tSeveral examples of cost-preserving preprocessing techniques are known. For practically all\n273\tof them, given a solution αP to the preprocessed instance (F, O + lb1 ), a solution α to the\n274\toriginal instance (FH , FS , w) for which cost(FS , w, α) ≤ αP (O) + lb1 can be obtained in\n275\tlinear time with respect to the number of clauses in FH ∪ FS [8, 25].\n276\t\n277\tThe Core-Guided Phase\n278\tThe next phase of core-boosted linear search applies core-guided search on the preprocessed\n279\tinstance (F, O + lb1 ). In the core-boosted setting, core-guided search only runs for a limited\n280\ttime. More precisely, the phase extracts a set cores of cores of (F, O + lb1 ) by repeated\n281\tinvocations of an incremental SAT solver in the way described in Section 2.2. When either\n282\tthe time limit for the core-guided phase is reached or no more cores can be found, the\n283\tcore-guided phase forms a new instance (F ∪ card, OR + lb2 ) by relaxing all cores in cores.\n284\tFor some informal intuition on core-guided search, we have that the difference lb2 − lb1 ≥ 0 is\n285\tequal to the minimum cost incurred by satisfying the cores in cores, and that the objective\n286\tOR measures the additional cost on top of satisfying the cores in cores that solutions of\n287\t(F ∪ card) incur in O. More precisely, we require that the core relaxation step is solution\n288\tpreserving in the sense of the next definition.\n289\t▶ Definition 4. Invoke the core-guided phase on the instance (F, O + lb1 ) and let (F ∪\n290\tcard, OR + lb2 ) be the instance returned. The core-guided phase is solution-preserving if the\n291\tfollowing conditions hold:\n292\t\n293\tCP 2025\n294\t\n295\t\f28:6\n296\t\n297\tSLS-Enhanced Core-Boosted Linear Search for Anytime Maximum Satisfiability\n298\t\n299\t(i) αR (OR ) + lb2 = αR (O) + lb1 for any solution αR to F ∪ card.\n300\t(ii) Any solution α to F can be extended into a solution αR to F ∪ card for which\n301\tαR (OR ) + lb2 = α(O) + lb1 .\n302\tIn practice, all core-guided algorithms for MaxSAT that we are aware of are solutionpreserving and can be used for core-boosted linear search. All of them implement the core\n303\trelaxation step by introducing new variables of form okC to OR as indicators for at least k ≥ 2\n304\tvariables in the core C being assigned to 1 by solutions of (F ∪ card). Essentially, such\n305\tvariables ensure that a solution to F ∪ card can assign one variable from each core to 1\n306\twithout incurring cost in OR , but need to assign one of the new variables to 1 (thus incurring\n307\tcost) for any subsequent ones. The additional clauses in card contain CNF encodings of\n308\tP\n309\treified cardinality constraints equivalent to ℓ∈C ℓ ≥ k → okC . While existing instantiations\n310\tof core-boosted search for MaxSAT only extract cores over original objective variables, in\n311\tthe general case, due to core relaxation changing the objective function, subsequent cores\n312\tcould also contain the new variables okC .\n313\t\n314\tThe Solution-Improving Phase\n315\tThe solution-improving phase is invoked on (F ∪ card, OR + lb2 ), the final working instance\n316\tof the core-guided phase. The phase looks for low-cost solutions of (F ∪ card, OR ) by\n317\tinvoking a SAT solver on the formula F ∪ card ∪ as-cnf(OR < αbest (OR )) where αbest is\n318\tthe current lowest-cost solution, and as-cnf(OR ≤ αbest (OR )) is a CNF encoding of the\n319\tobjective-improving constraint OR < αbest (OR ) that is satisfied by any solution α for which\n320\tα(OR ) < αbest (OR ). If the SAT solver returns a solution, it will cost less than αbest . Then,\n321\tthe objective-improving constraint is tightened, and the solver is invoked again. If, instead,\n322\tthe SAT solver determines that no such solution exists, the current best-known solution is\n323\treturned as optimal. The solution-improving phase runs until either an optimal solution\n324\tof (F ∪ card, OR ) is found, or a time-limit is reached, at which point, the solution α of\n325\tthe input clause-based instance (FH , FS , w) for which cost(FS , w, α) ≤ αbest (O) + lb1 is\n326\treturned.\n327\tAn essential intuition of core-boosted linear search is that any solution of F ∪ card\n328\tthat has a low-cost wrt OR + lb2 will correspond to a solution α of (FH , FS , w) for which\n329\tcost(FS , w, α) is low. This is because the core-guided phase is solution-preserving, and the\n330\tpreprocessing phase is cost-preserving. Next, we detail two additional heuristics designed for\n331\tany time solution-improving search that are important for our work.\n332\tIncreasing Precision. Solution-improving search with increasing precision [20] heuristically\n333\tpicks a constant ρ and runs solution-improving search on the objective Oρ = ⌊OR /ρ⌋ obtained\n334\tby: (i) dividing each coefficient in OR by ρ, (ii) rounding down, and (iii) removing all variables\n335\twith 0 coefficient. For some intuition on the name, notice how Oρ is a “lower precision”\n336\tapproximation of OR for which the solution improving constraint Oρ < αbest (Oρ ) can be\n337\tencoded with fewer clauses. While the division of an objective obviously can change the cost\n338\tof solutions, in practice it has been observed that solutions that have a low-cost wrt Oρ also\n339\ttend to have a low-cost wrt OR [20, 10]. If a minimum cost solution wrt Oρ is found, the value\n340\tof ρ is lowered – thus increasing the precision – and the search restarted. Solution-improving\n341\tsearch with increasing precision ends either when a minimum-cost solution of Oρ is found\n342\twhen ρ = 1, or when a time limit is reached.\n343\tPhase Saving. Phase saving refers to overriding the default polarity selection of the SAT\n344\tsolver to guide its search toward solutions of low cost. The intuition underlying phase saving\n345\tis that a SAT solver, in its default setting, aims to find any solution of its internal formula or\n346\t\n347\t\fO. Lübke and J. Berg\n348\t\n349\t28:7\n350\t\n351\tprove that one does not exist. In the context of anytime MaxSAT, not all solutions are equal,\n352\tso phase saving aims to ensure that the first solution that the solver finds is as low-cost as\n353\tpossible. Typical phase-saving schemes employed in anytime MaxSAT [3, 20, 38] involve\n354\tsetting the default polarity of the variables in the objective to not incur cost, and set the\n355\tpolarity of the remaining variables to match the current lowest-cost solution αbest .\n356\t\n357\t2.4\n358\t\n359\tStochastic Local Search for MaxSAT"}]},"uuid":"a2696868-be55-4ddc-b2a0-cc0efb8ee296","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:52:48.806Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c2eca0f9-4991-4795-b6ed-05de29498760","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a2696868-be55-4ddc-b2a0-cc0efb8ee296","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aec9dfe82ab5889ef","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01ABHv4A6Ryx6g5Gsu86vvCx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"关键发现：phase 切换是 **time limit**（每个 phase 有 time limit），不是 plateau detection。R13 推断的 \"plateau-based 动态阶段切换\" 是 transcript 自己加的解读，**不是 paper claim**。\n\n确认到这里，所有 8 条 claim 我都有数据。可以输出最终 audit。\n\n---\n\n## 8 条 claim audit 结果\n\n| # | claim | verdict | 备注 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | VeriPB CP'25 #21 Koops 等 7 作者《Practically Feasible Proof Logging for PB Optimization》 | **CONFIRMED** | LIPIcs vol.340 #21 (pages 21:1-21:27)。作者完全匹配（Koops/Le Berre/Myreen/Nordström/Oertel/Tan/Vinyals）。论文确实 claim 工业可用：\"performance ... now quite close to the level of SAT solving, and hence is clearly practically feasible\" |\n| 2 | PB Comp 2025 主 solver: Exact / PRINTEMPS / NaPS / SCIP；RoundingSat 唯一 unchecked deletion | **PARTIALLY** | Exact/PRINTEMPS/NaPS(+SCIP-NaPS)/SCIP/roundingsat 都列出，确认。但 transcript 漏列了 OR-Tools CP-SAT、Sat4j、UWrMaxSat、toulbar2 等同样参赛的 solver。\"RoundingSat 唯一 unchecked deletion\" 该 claim 在 PB25 主页查不到细节，cril 页面无证据，**未独立 verify** |\n| 3 | PB-OPT certificate 没有标准 ε-gap schema | **CONFIRMED** | PB Comp 2025 只有 PBS/PBO 两类带/不带 OPT/UNSAT 证书的 4 个 track，**无独立 dual-bound / ε-gap track**。这是核心 takeaway，对路线图最重要 |\n| 4 | cake_lpr 2026-02 升级 +5-10% 性能, binary -20% | **PARTIALLY** | WebSearch 摘要确认日期是 **2025-02-16**（非 2026-02）+5-10% 性能 / -20% binary。R13 transcript 写\"2026-02\"是年份打错（Claude 训练数据日期混淆），其他数字正确 |\n| 5 | Lübke & Berg, **CP'25** \"SLS-Enhanced Core-Boosted Linear Search for Anytime MaxSAT\" | **CONFIRMED** | CP'25 LIPIcs vol.340 #28，作者 Ole Lübke, Jeremias Berg。Transcript 内部一致写 CP'25。**用户路线图 commit 写的\"AAAI'25\"是抄错**，应改 CP'25 |\n| 6 | Bessa et al. **AAAI'25** \"Learning Valid Dual Bounds in CP\" | **CONFIRMED** | dblp `conf/aaai/BessaDBRC25`、AAAI proceedings vol.39 #11 pp.11113-11121。作者 Bessa/Dabert/Bourgeat/Rousseau/Cappart |\n| 7 | CP'24 Boudreault & Quimper《Multi-Stage Proof Logging Framework for CP Solvers》 | **REFUTED** | 论文标题确实存在（CP'24 LIPIcs vol.307 #11），但**作者完全错了**：实际是 **Flippo, Sidorov, Marijnissen, Smits, Demirović**（Delft 团队），与 Boudreault/Quimper 无关。Quimper 在 CP'24 是另一篇 #7\"Cumulative Scheduling with Calendars and Overtime\"（Cloutier 等）。R13 这里张冠李戴了 |\n| 8 | Bessa et al. arXiv 2408.12695 标题/abstract 匹配 | **CONFIRMED** | arXiv 2024-08-22 提交，标题完全一致，abstract 也吻合（learned Lagrangian multipliers via self-supervised NN） |\n\n## 关键修正\n\n1. **Lübke & Berg 是 CP'25，不是 AAAI'25**。Transcript 内部写 CP'25，路线图 commit 写 AAAI'25 是用户/我抄录时把它跟 Bessa AAAI'25 串了。所有 P2 #30 / commit message / 路线图条目里的 \"AAAI'25\" → 改 **\"CP'25\"**。\n\n2. **CP'24 multi-stage proof logging 作者是 Flippo et al.，不是 Boudreault & Quimper**。R13 transcript 这条直接把作者搞错（论文真实存在，但人物挂错了）。任何引用都要改作者。\n\n3. **\"plateau-based 动态阶段切换\" 不是 Lübke&Berg 的 claim**。我读了 paper 全文：CBLS 的三阶段切换机制是 **每个 phase 有独立 time limit**（\"core-guided search only runs for a limited time\"），**没有 plateau detection / stagnation trigger**。R13 transcript 那句\"核心切换时机由 plateau detect\"是 agent 自己延伸的解读 — 不能作为 P2 #30 新条目的 paper 依据。\n\n4. **cake_lpr 性能数字日期是 2025-02-16** 不是 2026-02-16（年份打错）。\n\n## 路线图修订建议\n\n- **R11 #6 VeriPB exporter 4-6h 工时**：维持有效。CP'25 #21 确实把 PB-OPT logging 推到 industrial，但 ε-gap intermediate cert 没标准 schema 这件事 confirmed → 自定义 transcoder 不可避免，4-6h 估时合理。\n- **P2 #30 plateau-based 动态阶段切换**：**修订引用**。不能挂 Lübke&Berg 当依据（paper 用 fixed time-limit per phase 不是 plateau）。条目本身的工程想法（Stage-2 提前进 Stage-3 if dual_growth_rate < threshold）有价值，但要标\"自创设计、无 paper 直接依据\"，去掉 Lübke&Berg 引用 — 或者 demote 到\"实验性 idea\"不是 paper-grounded 优化。\n- **\"中间 ε-gap 没标准 schema\" claim**：**维持有效**。PB25 track 列表已经核实，确实只有 OPT/UNSAT 证书，没 ε-gap track。\n\n## verdict\n\n**PARTIALLY** — 8 条里 4 条 CONFIRMED、2 条 PARTIALLY、1 条 REFUTED（CP'24 paper 作者搞错），还有一条衍生 claim（plateau-based）属于 R13 自加解读不是 paper claim。R13 的核心结论（VeriPB 工业可用 + ε-gap 无标准 + 4-6h 工时）站得住，但 P2 #30 新条目和 commit message 里的 \"Lübke&Berg AAAI'25\" 必须修。\n\n## 相关文件路径\n\n- Transcript: `/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd/docs/research/agent_transcripts/a3356c51d9d10daab.output`\n- Lübke&Berg PDF 转文字（验证用）: `/tmp/lubke_berg.txt`"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3306,"cache_read_input_tokens":46272,"output_tokens":2557,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3306},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2557,"cache_read_input_tokens":46272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3306,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CastrXS6oy9GsQGS8qJFX","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d2c3eba-6fd0-4313-ad35-b45ebc5ec80e","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:53:39.814Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
